  "captions": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "end": 6000,
      "text": "A neural network learns by adjusting the numbers inside it."
    },
    {
      "start": 6000,
      "end": 13000,
      "text": "Start with an example and its correct label. This tiny picture is a seven."
    },
    {
      "start": 13000,
      "end": 25000,
      "text": "Weighted sums, biases, and activations turn pixels into a prediction."
    },
    {
      "start": 25000,
      "end": 34000,
      "text": "Compare the score to the label. The loss measures how wrong the prediction is."
    },
    {
      "start": 34000,
      "end": 45000,
      "text": "Backpropagation works backward to calculate each parameter's gradient."
    },
    {
      "start": 45000,
      "end": 52000,
      "text": "Gradient descent takes a small step: old weight minus step size times gradient."
    },
    {
      "start": 52000,
      "end": 55000,
      "text": "With updated weights and biases, this example gets a better score."
    },
    {
      "start": 55000,
      "end": 64000,
      "text": "Repeat across examples, and check separate data to see what the model learned."
    },
    {
      "start": 64000,
      "end": 72000,
      "text": "Guess. Measure. Adjust. Repeat. Then test whether the learning carries over."
    }
  ],
